# Exercise: Sleeping
#
# `time.sleep-ms` pauses the current sequence for *at least* N
# milliseconds. The OS may schedule you back later than that, but
# never sooner.
#
# Stack effect: ( Int -- )
#
#   1000 time.sleep-ms    # block for one second
#   5    time.sleep-ms    # block for five milliseconds
#
# Heads up: the unit is fixed at milliseconds — there is no
# `time.sleep` or `time.sleep-secs`. Multiply by 1000 if you want
# whole seconds.
#
# Your task: write `tiny-pause` — sleep for 5 milliseconds and
# then push `true`. The Bool gives the test something to assert,
# and the test only passes if the word reached the end (i.e. the
# sleep actually returned).
#
# When done, delete the marker line below.

# I AM NOT DONE

: tiny-pause ( -- Bool )
    # Your code here
    false
;

: test-sleep ( -- )
    tiny-pause

    # Do not edit below this line
    test.assert
;
